            <ArticleTitle>&quot;Candy wrapper&quot; effect after drug-eluting stent implantation: déjà vu or stumbling over the same stone again?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>387-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Encouraging results have been obtained with drug-eluting stents (DESs) to prevent restenosis following PCI. However, DESs are not immune from restenosis and we describe a case of &quot;candy wrapper&quot; effect, commonly observed with intracoronary brachytherapy (IBT). In this article, we review the common drawbacks of DES and IBT and their prevention.</AbstractText>
